  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. Running the function directly also gives 480.\n\nIt only calls two modules: `pricing` and `discounts`.\n\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = 600\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` uses a 20% discount: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = 480\n\nNothing imports `decoy_tax.py` or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't change the result. The gold tax rate of 25% in `decoy_tax.py` isn't used.\n\nANSWER: 480",
